note mistake_bound_input: a bound is a trap, not a clamp. scan counts letters with bound 70; the 111
note letters stand for outside input (a request line, a file, a database row): pass 71 traps 4, exit 104.
note The fix is bound_input_guard.om: stop below the bound, or check the length before the loop.
global b uchar 128
fn scan e ulong to ulong
q = ulong 0
while lt q e bound 70
if ne get b q 65
break
end
q = add q 1
end
ret q
end
fn main to int
for i ulong 111
put b i 65
end
r = scan ulong 111
if eq r 0
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
